carlhnelson@gmail.com wrote:
> Does anyone have any suggestions for the "slogging through Gehennom"
> portion of the game?  Without a lot of experience I've taken to
> painstakingly clearing those levels out because I'm afraid of not being
> able to move through them fast enough on my way back out.  Do seasoned
> players avoid this?
> 
I tend to do painstaking clearing downwards until I find Vlad's tower, then 
I teleport to the bottom, find the VS, mark it (by breaking a WoDig) and 
try to chase something that teleports to the stairs and escapes up them.

Then once the down and up routes meet I'll probably teleport back up to my 
cache, get ready for the final run, then teleport back down to the wizard's 
tower entrance.

Orcus town is also best handled by finding it on the way down then going to 
the level below and returning up the stairs with a rubber chicken.

Digging between the stairs on at least some of the levels helps (but not 
much if you keep getting pushed back down). Lots of wands of teleport also 
help if you find your way to the stairs blocked (but keep a good number for 
the planes).


